# Put the KSU autoinstall script where KernelSU will run it.
#
# init deliberately does NOT exec anything here. A service like
#   service ksu_autoinstall /system/bin/sh /system_ext/bin/ksu-autoinstall.sh
# fails with "File /system/bin/sh (labeled u:object_r:shell_exec:s0) has
# incorrect label or no domain transition from u:r:init:s0", because init may
# not exec a shell without a domain of its own. `copy` is a built-in init
# command, so it needs no exec and no new sepolicy.
#
# KernelSU runs everything in /data/adb/boot-completed.d in its own context
# (u:r:ksu:s0) -- the same context ksud itself runs in, which is what
# `ksud module install` needs. It must be that stage and not service.d:
# `ksud module install` refuses with "Android is Booting!" until boot is
# complete, and the services stage runs well before that.
#
# system_ext, not vendor: a vendor rc runs as vendor_init and cannot touch
# /data/adb.
#
# The copy happens on every boot so an updated ROM refreshes the script; the
# script itself is idempotent through its markers.

on post-fs-data
    mkdir /data/adb 0700 root root

    # Seed ksud. On a wiped device /data/adb/ksud does not exist until the
    # manager app is opened, and without it KernelSU is completely inert:
    #   init: Command 'exec u:r:ksu:s0 root -- /data/adb/ksud post-fs-data'
    #         failed: Cannot find '/data/adb/ksud'
    # ...and the same for `services` and `boot-completed`. Since boot-completed
    # is what runs boot-completed.d, the script below could never run either, so
    # seeding from inside it was circular. init must do it.
    #
    # This is the same binary the manager would copy, shipped in this ROM, so it
    # matches this kernel. It is rewritten every boot, which also repairs a
    # deleted or truncated ksud.
    #
    # KSU's own post-fs-data exec (init.rc) runs before this one, so on the very
    # first boot after a wipe that stage is still skipped -- harmless, as there
    # are no modules to mount yet. `services` and `boot-completed` come later and
    # do find it.
    copy /product/app/KernelSUNext/lib/arm64/libksud.so /data/adb/ksud
    chmod 0755 /data/adb/ksud
    chown root root /data/adb/ksud

    mkdir /data/adb/boot-completed.d 0700 root root
    copy /system_ext/bin/ksu-autoinstall.sh /data/adb/boot-completed.d/ksu-autoinstall.sh
    chmod 0700 /data/adb/boot-completed.d/ksu-autoinstall.sh
    chown root root /data/adb/boot-completed.d/ksu-autoinstall.sh
